  "lower_bound_argument": "OBJECT-DECOMPOSITION CLOSED FORM, mechanised twice by two independent implementations (<path>/prove2.py fast+pruned, <path>/prove.py unpruned) which agree on all six levels. OBJECTS = the level's position-groups: a lone sprite (mode = position x rotation) or a CAROUSEL of sprites sharing one position with exactly one member visible (mode = position x visible-member index; a stacked sprite can never be rotated because ACTION5 on a stacked selection cycles instead of rotating). (1) EVERY engine action changes the mode of AT MOST ONE object: ACTION1-4 translate only the selected sprite (bounds-checked), ACTION5 rotates the selected lone sprite then clamps or cycles the selected carousel then clamps, ACTION6 changes the SELECTION and may additionally cycle the selected carousel (when the clicked pixel of the selected stacked sprite renders 0) -- note that this click-cycle edge is real and is INCLUDED, it is not a selection-only action. (2) The selected OBJECT changes only at an ACTION6 that is not a cycle (a cycle re-selects a member of the SAME object). Hence, with S = {o : C_o != start_o} and o0 the initially selected object, L = #clicks + #non-clicks >= sum_o d_o(start_o -> C_o) + |S| - [o0 in S]. (3) Every d_o is an exact BFS over that object's own complete graph; the edge set used is a SUPERSET of the real one (the ping-pong direction flag is global and is treated as free, and both the clamped ACTION5-cycle and the unclamped click-cycle results are edges), so each d_o under-estimates -- the safe direction. (4) The configuration enumeration is COMPLETE: the engine wins iff, for each joint kind k in {8,13} SEPARATELY, every cell carrying a kind-k joint of a VISIBLE sprite carries exactly two (read directly off sjwqloivve/uqlndqojuf). So every winning configuration induces a perfect matching of the kind-k joints, and we enumerate all identity choices (lone rotation / carousel member) x all perfect matchings x all free translations of every connected component of the induced offset-constraint graph, solved by union-find with offsets. Configurations where a cell carries FOUR joints are admitted too (a strict SUPERSET of the win set), which only weakens the bound. (5) ACTION7 is inert (no branch for it in Cn04.step) -- verified empirically at all 173 states along the six routes. RESET cannot shorten a win: it restores the level start without any win check, so any winning play containing a reset is 1 + (a winning play from the level start) and is strictly longer than the reset-free minimum. ARGMIN configuration for L1: (3,3,rot90) + (2,8,rot90).",
